dho:p-sn46.20-1.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.20 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.20:1.1" ;
    dho:textEn "“Mendicants, the seven awakening factors, when developed and cultivated, lead solely to disillusionment, dispassion, cessation, peace, insight, awakening, and extinguishment."@en ;
    dho:textPi "“Sattime, bhikkhave, bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā ekantanibbidāya virāgāya nirodhāya upasamāya abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattanti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.20/en/sujato#sn46.20:1.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.20-1.4 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.20 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.20:1.4" ;
    dho:textEn "These seven awakening factors, when developed and cultivated, lead solely to disillusionment, dispassion, cessation, peace, insight, awakening, and extinguishment.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "ime kho, bhikkhave, satta bojjhaṅgā bhāvitā bahulīkatā ekantanibbidāya virāgāya nirodhāya upasamāya abhiññāya sambodhāya nibbānāya saṁvattantī”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.20/en/sujato#sn46.20:1.4"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-10.1 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:10.1" ;
    dho:textEn "And what is the way in which the seven awakening factors become fourteen?"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Katamo ca, bhikkhave, pariyāyo, yaṁ pariyāyaṁ āgamma satta bojjhaṅgā catuddasa honti?"@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:10.1"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:p-sn46.52-16.3 a dho:Passage ;
    dho:inText dho:t-sn46.52 ;
    dho:segment "sn46.52:16.3" ;
    dho:textEn "This is the way in which the seven awakening factors become fourteen.”"@en ;
    dho:textPi "Ayaṁ kho, bhikkhave, pariyāyo, yaṁ pariyāyaṁ āgamma satta bojjhaṅgā catuddasā”ti."@pi ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.52/en/sujato#sn46.52:16.3"^^xsd:anyURI .

dho:t-sn46.28 a dho:Text ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dct:source "SuttaCentral bilara-data: English by Bhikkhu Sujato, Pali Mahāsaṅgīti edition" ;
    skos:prefLabel "SN 46.28 Nibbedhabhāgiyasutta — Helping Penetration"@en ;
    dho:coverage dho:PartlyEncoded ;
    dho:encodes "The seven factors are the path that helps penetration (1.1, 1.5, 1.9, 2.9); the list (1.7); the stock formula for each factor (relies on seclusion, fading away and cessation; ripens as letting go) (2.1, 2.5)." ;
    dho:layer dho:SuttaLayer ;
    dho:leftOut "With a mind that has developed each factor, they penetrate and shatter the mass of greed, hate and delusion for the first time (2.2-2.4, 2.6-2.8); 'weakens' would understate 'shatter', so it waits for a better fit. Also 'abundant, expansive, limitless, and free of ill will' (2.1, 2.5)." ;
    dho:modelledBy "project owner with Claude (AI assistant), from SuttaCentral's text" ;
    dho:modelledOn "2026-11-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dho:review dho:Unreviewed ;
    dho:url "https://suttacentral.net/sn46.28/en/sujato"^^xsd:anyURI .

